cache
__pycache__
.venv
.vscode/
# Local secrets (MAPILLARY_ACCESS_TOKEN, PS_INTERNAL_API_KEY) — never commit.
.env
*.jsonl
*.submitted
nohup.out
smoke_check

# Run directories: track only the small, high-value files (provenance + hand-labeled
# verdicts); results and resume caches stay local.
runs/**
!runs/*/
!runs/*/manifest.json
!runs/*/area.geojson
!runs/*/*_verdicts.json
!runs/*/*.submission.json
# Position check (position_check.py, run by main.py at the end of every run): the verdict
# and its self-contained report stay with the run's provenance — including the
# <stem>.position_check.json written beside a repositioned submission, since its
# *.submission.json is tracked and the verdict it shipped under must be too. The
# reposition output itself and the Overpass cache beside them are not.
!runs/*/position_check.json
!runs/*/position_report.html
!runs/*/*.position_check.json
!runs/*/*.position_report.html
# Server-side clustering evaluation (scripts/eval_ps_clustering.py, protocol and
# findings in docs/ps-clustering-eval.md): the report and its per-arm CSV are the
# study's evidence, small and stable, so they are tracked like manifest.json. The
# two API pulls they are computed from are NOT — tens of MB apiece — so the report
# carries each one's url, fetch time, sha256 and feature count instead.
!runs/*/ps_clustering_eval*/
!runs/*/ps_clustering_eval*/report.md
!runs/*/ps_clustering_eval*/arms.csv
# Camera-rig labels already live on a server (detectors.on_camera_rig; see the nadir-mask
# section of CLAUDE.md). These are the evidence base for the mask AND the exact set a
# cleanup would retire, so they have to outlive both the database state and the API pull
# they were derived from — the file records that pull's url and sha256 for the tie-back.
!runs/*/rig_labels.json
# Per-rig camera heights for Mapillary runs (scripts/mapillary_height.py, issue #53): the
# table `fuse_sites.py --camera-height-m per-rig` reads, bound to results.jsonl by sha256.
!runs/*/camera_heights.json
# The #87 height-gap study (scripts/height_gap.py; docs/mapillary-camera-height.md section 7):
# its CSVs and report are the evidence and are tracked. camera_height/groups.csv stays local.
!runs/*/camera_height/
!runs/*/camera_height/estimator_validation.csv
!runs/*/camera_height/estimator_validation_seeds.csv
!runs/*/camera_height/estimator_validation_exploratory.csv
# ...but the cross-city _summary copies stay local (regenerated by every run)
runs/_summary/camera_height/estimator_validation*.csv
!runs/*/camera_height/gap/
!runs/*/camera_height/gap/*.csv
!runs/*/camera_height/gap/report.md
# AI-vs-crowd agree rate (scripts/agree_rate.py, write-up in docs/agree-rate-<city>.md): the
# report and CSVs are the evidence and are tracked. The three API pulls they are computed
# from (the frozen crowd snapshot) are NOT — the report carries each one's url, fetch time,
# sha256 and feature count instead.
!runs/*/agree_rate/
!runs/*/agree_rate/report.md
!runs/*/agree_rate/*.csv
# Server-side validations + one auditor vs the AI (scripts/server_agree_check.py): report and
# CSVs tracked; the four API pulls are NOT -- the report carries url, fetch time, sha256, count.
# Except Laurens's (2.4 MB, as #113 tracked Gainesville's): its auditor numbers went to
# RampNet#158 and the live server moves within the hour, so the pull is the only way to
# re-score them from git. Richmond (22 MB) and Vancouver (84 MB) stay untracked.
!runs/*/server_agree/
!runs/*/server_agree/report.md
!runs/*/server_agree/*.csv
!runs/laurens/server_agree/*.geojson
!runs/laurens/server_agree/*.geojson.source.json
# The pulls as served (full human user ids) live only here, never tracked: the script
# writes a redacted copy beside it and refuses to use an unredacted pull at a tracked path.
runs/*/server_agree/as_served/
# Label-frame beta (scripts/label_frame_beta.py, issue #113): the report and CSVs are
# tracked. Unlike the rule above, Gainesville's API pull (5.2 MB) is tracked too: the live
# API cannot return the same snapshot later, so without it the committed result could not
# be re-scored from git. The report's url, fetch time and sha256 tie it back.
!runs/*/label_frame_beta/
!runs/*/label_frame_beta/report.md
!runs/*/label_frame_beta/*.csv
!runs/gainesville/label_frame_beta/raw_labels_CurbRamp.geojson
!runs/gainesville/label_frame_beta/raw_labels_CurbRamp.geojson.source.json
# The vouched-pool run's own inputs and outputs, so it can be re-scored without a GPU and
# re-run from git: the pano list, the detections (3.4 MB, 2.8 GPU-hours), their meta, and the
# runner + log that made them. The pano-tools CSVs stay out: they are pinned by commit+sha256.
!runs/_pooled/label_frame_beta/pool_ids.txt
!runs/_pooled/label_frame_beta/pool_detections.jsonl
!runs/_pooled/label_frame_beta/pool_detections.jsonl.meta.json
!runs/_pooled/label_frame_beta/pool_detect.py
!runs/_pooled/label_frame_beta/pool_detect.log
# Post-submission coverage check (scripts/coverage_check.py, issue #46): the report and its
# gap lists (missing.csv, fallback.csv) are tracked. The three API pulls are NOT — the report
# carries each one's url, fetch time, sha256 and row count instead.
!runs/*/coverage/
!runs/*/coverage/report.md
!runs/*/coverage/*.csv
# DEM road grade (scripts/dem_grade.py, #51; write-up in docs/dem-grade-study.md): the tile
# manifest (service, request, per-tile sha256) and the agreement report are tracked. The
# tiles themselves (tens to hundreds of MB) and grades.csv are NOT — the report carries
# grades.csv's sha256, and tiles.json is enough to refetch and verify every tile.
!runs/*/dem/
!runs/*/dem/tiles.json
!runs/*/dem/report.md
# Per-pano camera-height QC tests (scripts/height_qc.py, issue #44; write-up in
# docs/camera-height-study.md): the pre-registered verdicts and their tables are tracked.
# runs/_pooled/height_qc/ holds the cross-city verdicts the rule in depth.py follows.
!runs/*/height_qc/
!runs/*/height_qc/report.md
!runs/*/height_qc/*.csv
# External placement oracle (scripts/inventory_oracle.py, issue #79; write-up in
# docs/placement-oracle.md): the city inventory's provenance record (url, query, fetch
# time, sha256, counts) and the scored tables are tracked. The inventory pull itself
# (inventory.geojson) is NOT -- inventory.json carries its sha256 and the query to refetch it.
!runs/*/inventory_oracle/
!runs/*/inventory_oracle/report.md
!runs/*/inventory_oracle/*.csv
!runs/*/inventory_oracle/inventory.json
# Clustering scored against those inventories (scripts/inventory_clustering.py, #106 Part 2;
# pre-registration and findings in docs/ps-clustering-eval.md): the per-city report and
# per-arm CSV, and the pooled verdict, are tracked. The street-network pull used for regions
# (streets.geojson) is NOT -- the report carries its url, fetch time, sha256 and count.
!runs/*/inventory_clustering/
!runs/*/inventory_clustering/report.md
!runs/*/inventory_clustering/*.csv
!runs/_pooled/inventory_clustering/verdict.json
# The pooled clustering eval over every benchmark city (scripts/clustering_eval_pooled.py,
# #106 Part 1): report.md is covered by the ps_clustering_eval* rule above; its two tables
# are tracked too. The per-run street pulls (runs/<run>/ps_streets.geojson) are NOT.
!runs/_pooled/ps_clustering_eval/*.csv
# GSV partial pose (scripts/gsv_partial_pose.py, issue #116; write-up in
# docs/gsv-partial-pose-study.md): per-city report + CSVs and the pooled coefficients,
# verdict and summary are the evidence and are tracked.
!runs/*/partial_pose/
!runs/*/partial_pose/*.md
!runs/*/partial_pose/*.csv
!runs/*/partial_pose/explore_full/
!runs/*/partial_pose/explore_full/*.md
!runs/*/partial_pose/explore_full/*.csv
# ...and the #116 confirmatory run (`gsv_partial_pose.py confirm`; an --exploratory run
# writes confirm_exploratory_<height>/ and is labelled so in every file).
!runs/*/partial_pose/confirm_*/
!runs/*/partial_pose/confirm_*/*.md
!runs/*/partial_pose/confirm_*/*.csv
!runs/*/partial_pose/confirm_*/*.json
# Provenance gate (scripts/provenance_gate.py, issue #56): does a run rebuilt from the pano
# store reproduce the city's deployed AI labels? The report and the unmatched-label rows are
# tracked; the label pull (raw_labels.geojson) is NOT -- the report carries its url, fetch
# time, sha256 and feature count.
!runs/*/provenance_gate/
!runs/*/provenance_gate/report.md
!runs/*/provenance_gate/unmatched.csv
# ...and the control arm's pano ids (--draw-control), drawn with a fixed seed.
!runs/*/provenance_gate/control_ids.txt
# The rebuilt run's definition (scripts/detect_from_store.py, #56): the selection record
# (inputs' sha256, seed, store, layout, server, id-list sha256) and the sampled unlabeled
# stratum are tracked, so the empty stratum can be rebuilt from git after the store grows.
# store_ids.txt (the full list, ~700 KB) is NOT: its labeled part is the label pull's.
!runs/*/store_selection.json
!runs/*/store_sampled_ids.txt
# A store-bound depth dir's record (harvest_depth.py --from-store): which store, and the
# live frame check's result. The index itself stays untracked, as for a harvest.
!runs/*/depth/
!runs/*/depth/store.json
# Aerial sidewalk study (scripts/aerial_sidewalks.py, issue #104; write-up in
# docs/aerial-sidewalk-study.md): the Tile2Net provenance record (tile source, zoom, commit,
# runtime, tile count, polygon sha256), the tile audit (tile_audit.json, blank_tiles.csv), the
# hole breakdown (holes.json, holes.csv), the reports and the CSVs are tracked. The polygons
# and network themselves (polygons.geojson, network.geojson) and the gallery (pixels) are NOT.
!runs/*/aerial/
!runs/*/aerial/tile2net.json
!runs/*/aerial/tile_audit.json
!runs/*/aerial/holes.json
!runs/*/aerial/report*.md
!runs/*/aerial/*.csv
!runs/_summary/
!runs/_summary/aerial/
!runs/_summary/aerial/*.csv
!runs/_summary/aerial/verdict.json
# RampNet#158 phase 2: placement arms' per-candidate predictions (copied from RampNet's
# analysis_out/mined_placement_158/predictions/), the input to mined_precision.py --placement.
!docs/figures/mined-precision/data/placement/*.jsonl
# RampNet#158 step 3: the richmond / bend floor re-inference over judged panos (small).
!docs/figures/mined-precision/data/step3/*.jsonl
# Footway: segmenter vs GSV depth (scripts/footway_segmentation.py, issue #47 step 2; write-up
# in docs/footway-depth-study.md): per-city and pooled reports, CSVs, the verdict and the
# label-map manifest are tracked. The tiles and label maps (runs/_pooled/footway/work/) are
# NOT -- masks_manifest.json carries the model revision and every label map's sha256.
!runs/*/footway/
!runs/*/footway/report.md
!runs/*/footway/*.csv
!runs/*/footway/*.json
